"    df1['final_price'],\n","    bins=40,\n","    kde=True,\n","    color='#00f2ff',      # Neon Cyan\n","    edgecolor='#121212',  # Contrast edge\n","    alpha=0.7,\n","    line_kws={'lw': 3}    # Thicker KDE line\n",")\n","\n","# 4. Styling Labels and Titles for Visibility (White/Grey)\n","plt.title('3.d Univariate: Product Price Distribution', fontsize=18, fontweight='bold', pad=25, color='#ffffff')\n","plt.xlabel('Final Price ($)', fontsize=12, color='#cccccc', labelpad=10)\n","plt.ylabel('Frequency (Count)', fontsize=12, color='#cccccc', labelpad=10)\n","\n","# 5. Adjusting Tick Colors\n","plt.xticks(color='#888888')\n","plt.yticks(color='#888888')\n","\n","# Remove borders for a \"Floating\" modern look\n","sns.despine(left=True, bottom=True)\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":601},"id":"MW73ntfvotdF","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786721279476,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":852,"user":{"displayName":"anu mol tp","userId":"01105894824813683102"}},"outputId":"3280f2ba-5e8f-4ab4-a47c-93e9d1700a58"},"execution_count":41,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **3.e Category Volume Analysis (Bar Chart)**\n","**Objective:** To identify which product categories have the most listings and dominate the inventory."],"metadata":{"id":"z3Kl_2Mno1Jy"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **Key Insights**\n","\n","\n","*  **Volume Check:** Shows which categories take up the most space in your catalog.\n","\n","*  **Operational Focus:** Higher listing counts usually mean more effort needed for inventory management and support.\n","\n","*  **Precision:** Includes exact counts at the end of each bar for quick data reading\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"FzfTwItao8sq"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import seaborn as sns\n","\n","# 1. Set the Dark Theme for the Analyst Dashboard\n","sns.set_theme(style=\"darkgrid\", rc={\"axes.facecolor\": \"#121212\", \"grid.color\": \"#222222\"})\n","\n","# 2. Setup Figure with Black Background\n","plt.figure(figsize=(12, 7), facecolor=\"#121212\")\n","ax = plt.gca()\n","\n","# 3. Data Preparation\n","category_order = df1['category'].value_counts().index\n","counts = df1['category'].value_counts()\n","\n","# 4. Create Horizontal Count Plot (Using 'mako' for a sleek neon teal/blue gradient)\n","sns.countplot(\n","    data=df1,\n","    y='category',\n","    order=category_order,\n","    palette='mako',\n","    hue='category',\n","    legend=False\n",")\n","\n","# 5. Add exact count labels in High-Contrast Neon Green\n","for i, v in enumerate(counts):\n","    ax.text(v + (max(counts)*0.01), i, str(v), color='#adff2f',\n","            va='center', fontweight='bold', fontsize=11)\n","\n","# 6. Styling Labels and Titles for Visibility\n","plt.title('3.e Univariate: Inventory Volume per Category',\n","          fontsize=18, fontweight='bold', pad=25, color='#ffffff')\n","plt.xlabel('Number of Listings', fontsize=12, color='#cccccc', labelpad=10)\n","plt.ylabel('Product Category', fontsize=12, color='#cccccc', labelpad=10)\n","\n","# 7. Adjusting Ticks\n","plt.xticks(color='#888888')\n","plt.yticks(color='#ffffff', fontsize=10)\n","\n","# 8. Remove borders for a \"Floating\" modern look\n","sns.despine(left=True, bottom=True)\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()\n"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":701},"id":"37EXAp_yrAyN","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786721284640,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":385,"user":{"displayName":"anu mol tp","userId":"01105894824813683102"}},"outputId":"06bfdbe1-293d-48dd-ca4b-4eeda829c69d"},"execution_count":42,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1200x700 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **3.f Rating Distribution Analysis (Boxplot)**\n","**Objective:** To visualize the spread, median, and potential outliers in customer ratings across the entire dataset."],"metadata":{"id":"uVl590c0rROD"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **Key Insights**\n","\n","\n","\n","*  **Median Rating:** The central line inside the \"notch\" shows the average customer sentiment.\n","*  **Consistency:** The width of the box indicates how consistent the ratings are; a smaller box means ratings are closely grouped.\n","\n","* **Outliers:** The dots (fliers) identify products with unusually low or high ratings compared to the rest of the inventory.\n","\n","\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"6RnDHgjQrYO8"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import seaborn as sns\n","\n","# 1. Set the Dark Theme for the Analyst Dashboard\n","sns.set_theme(style=\"darkgrid\", rc={\"axes.facecolor\": \"#121212\", \"grid.color\": \"#222222\"})\n","\n","# 2. Setup Figure with Black Background\n","plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5), facecolor=\"#121212\")\n","ax = plt.gca()\n","\n","# 3. Create the Notched Boxplot\n","# Using Neon Gold (#e9c46a) for the box and light grey for outliers\n","sns.boxplot(\n","    x=df1['rating'],\n","    color='#e9c46a',\n","    width=0.4,\n","    linewidth=2.5,\n","    notch=True,\n","    fliersize=6,\n","    flierprops={\"marker\": \"o\", \"markerfacecolor\": \"#ff4d4d\", \"markeredgecolor\": \"none\", \"alpha\": 0.6}\n",")\n","\n","# 4. Styling Labels and Titles for Visibility\n","plt.title('3.f Univariate: Overall Rating Distribution & Quality Spread',\n","          fontsize=18, fontweight='bold', pad=25, color='#ffffff')\n","plt.xlabel('Customer Rating (1-5 Stars)', fontsize=12, color='#cccccc', labelpad=15)\n","\n","# 5. Adjusting Ticks\n","plt.xticks(color='#ffffff', fontweight='bold')\n","\n","# 6. Remove borders for a \"Floating\" modern look\n","sns.despine(left=True, bottom=True)\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":501},"id":"T48dN_69r2YY","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786721291344,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":527,"user":{"displayName":"anu mol tp","userId":"01105894824813683102"}},"outputId":"747459e3-f691-43e4-d464-4bd90f2f686b"},"execution_count":43,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x500 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **3.g Category Share Analysis (Donut Chart)**\n","**Objective:** To visualize the proportional share of each product category within the total inventory."],"metadata":{"id":"BG7E25iDr7lf"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **Key Insights**\n","\n","\n","*  Market Composition: Highlights which categories dominate the store's overall catalog.\n","*  Proportionality: Provides a clear view of how diversified the product range is.\n","\n","*  Percentage Share: Shows the relative size of each category using precise percentages\n"],"metadata":{"id":"XOjG-wj9sAjl"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import seaborn as sns\n","\n","# 1. Setup the Figure with a Black Background\n","plt.figure(figsize=(9, 9), facecolor=\"#121212\")\n","counts = df1['category'].value_counts()\n","\n","# 2. Create the Pie/Donut segments\n","# Using 'Spectral' palette with a slightly higher contrast for dark mode\n","patches, texts, autotexts = plt.pie(\n","    counts,\n","    labels=counts.index,\n","    autopct='%1.1f%%',\n","    startangle=140,\n","    colors=sns.color_palette(\"Spectral\", len(counts)),\n","    pctdistance=0.85,\n","    wedgeprops={'edgecolor': '#121212', 'linewidth': 3} # Dark edges for separation\n",")\n","\n","# 3. Styling the text for High Visibility\n","# Label text (Outside)\n","for text in texts:\n","    text.set_color('#ffffff')\n","    text.set_weight('bold')\n","    text.set_fontsize(11)\n","\n","# Percentage text (Inside)\n","for autotext in autotexts:\n","    autotext.set_color('#121212') # Dark text on bright segments for readability\n","    autotext.set_weight('bold')\n","    autotext.set_fontsize(10)\n","\n","# 4. Create the 'Donut' hole (Matching the dark background)\n","centre_circle = plt.Circle((0,0), 0.70, fc=\"#121212\")\n","plt.gca().add_artist(centre_circle)\n","\n","# 5. Title and Final Formatting\n","plt.title('3.g Univariate: Percentage Share of Categories',\n","          fontsize=20, fontweight='bold', pad=25, color='#ffffff')\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":901},"id":"DfNccfw2sY9a","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786721298005,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":470,"user":{"displayName":"anu mol tp","userId":"01105894824813683102"}},"outputId":"ff135766-b00e-4d41-de4d-79aba5a2877b"},"execution_count":44,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 900x900 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **3.h Bivariate Analysis: Price vs. Rating Hexbin Density**\n","**Objective:** To analyze the relationship between product pricing and customer satisfaction using hexagonal binning. This method aggregates data points into hexagonal cells, where the color intensity represents the frequency of products, providing a clearer view of data concentration than a standard scatter plot."],"metadata":{"id":"R8Scs1pfsoBn"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **Key Insights**\n","\n","\n","\n","*  **Density Identification:** Darker/Brighter hexagons identify the exact price range where the highest volume of products consistently receives specific ratings.\n","\n","*  **Marginal Distributions:** The integrated histograms on the top and right axes allow for a simultaneous univariate check, showing the volume of inventory at each price point and rating level.\n","\n","* **Handling Large Data:** Unlike scatter plots which can become \"noisy\" with 20,000+ rows, the Hexbin plot provides a clean, summarized view of where the business is most active"],"metadata":{"id":"0hq9KT82s0cR"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import seaborn as sns\n","\n","# 1. Set the Dark Theme for the Analyst Dashboard\n","sns.set_theme(style=\"darkgrid\", rc={\"axes.facecolor\": \"#121212\", \"grid.color\": \"#222222\"})\n","\n","# 2. Creating the Hexbin JointPlot\n","# Using 'magma' for a \"lava/glow\" effect on a dark background\n","g = sns.jointplot(\n","    data=df1,\n","    x='final_price',\n","    y='rating',\n","    kind='hex',\n","    cmap='magma',\n","    height=8,\n","    marginal_kws=dict(bins=30, fill=True, color='#fb8500') # Neon Orange marginals\n",")\n","\n","# 3. Styling the Figure and Background\n","g.fig.set_facecolor(\"#121212\")\n","g.fig.subplots_adjust(top=0.9)\n","\n","# 4. Titles and Labels for Visibility\n","g.fig.suptitle('3.h Bivariate: Price vs. Rating Density (Hexbin)',\n","               fontsize=18, fontweight='bold', color='#ffffff', y=0.95)\n","\n","g.set_axis_labels('Final Price ($)', 'Customer Rating (1-5)', color='#cccccc', fontsize=12)\n","\n","# 5. Adjusting Tick Colors for Dark Mode\n","for ax in [g.ax_joint, g.ax_marg_x, g.ax_marg_y]:\n","    ax.tick_params(colors='#888888')\n","\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":778},"id":"1sh1XdaLtLy0","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786721305475,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":1227,"user":{"displayName":"anu mol tp","userId":"01105894824813683102"}},"outputId":"d8427056-ae7f-4131-982e-04f0316a9178"},"execution_count":45,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 800x800 with 3 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["\n","# **3.i Price Distribution Across Categories (Boxplot)**\n","**Objective:** To compare the pricing structure and variations across different product categories."],"metadata":{"id":"Gh2VqyvutSni"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **Key Insights**\n","\n","\n","*  **Price Variance:** Shows which categories have a wide range of prices versus those that are more consistent.\n","\n","*   **tegory Comparison:** Easily identifies which categories are \"Premium\" (higher median) and which are \"Budget\" (lower median).\n","\n","*  **Outliers:** Highlights specific products within categories that are priced significantly higher than the average for that group.\n","\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"aX4FEaXMtYRw"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import seaborn as sns\n","\n","# 1. Set the Dark Theme for the Analyst Dashboard\n","sns.set_theme(style=\"darkgrid\", rc={\"axes.facecolor\": \"#121212\", \"grid.color\": \"#222222\"})\n","\n","# 2. Setup Figure with Black Background\n","plt.figure(figsize=(12, 8), facecolor=\"#121212\")\n","ax = plt.gca()\n","\n","# 3. Create Horizontal Box Plot\n","# Adding hue='category' and legend=False fixes the Seaborn palette warning\n","sns.boxplot(\n","    data=df1,\n","    x='final_price',\n","    y='category',\n","    hue='category',\n","    palette='magma',\n","    width=0.6,\n","    legend=False,\n","    linewidth=2,\n","    flierprops={\"marker\": \"x\", \"markerfacecolor\": \"#ff4d4d\", \"markeredgecolor\": \"#ff4d4d\", \"alpha\": 0.5}\n",")\n","\n","# 4. Styling Labels and Titles for Visibility\n","plt.title('3.i Bivariate: Price Distribution Across Categories',\n","          fontsize=18, fontweight='bold', pad=25, color='#ffffff')\n","plt.xlabel('Product Price ($)', fontsize=12, color='#cccccc', labelpad=15)\n","plt.ylabel('Product Category', fontsize=12, color='#cccccc')\n","\n","# 5. Adjusting Ticks and Grid\n","plt.xticks(color='#888888')\n","plt.yticks(color='#ffffff', fontsize=10)\n","plt.grid(axis='x', linestyle='--', alpha=0.1)\n","\n","# 6. Remove borders for a \"Floating\" modern look\n","sns.despine(left=True, bottom=True)\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":801},"id":"PZJE3TiKuIIP","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786721310387,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":651,"user":{"displayName":"anu mol tp","userId":"01105894824813683102"}},"outputId":"47a3f45c-dcdf-447c-f031-7ad0d975b71b"},"execution_count":46,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1200x800 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **3.j Category Performance Analysis (Lollipop Chart)**\n","**Objective:** To rank and compare the average customer satisfaction (Rating) across different business categories using a modern, minimalist visual. This helps in identifying which segments are meeting customer expectations and which require quality improvements."],"metadata":{"id":"p_WD79cYudBa"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **Key Insights**\n","\n","*  **Quality Leaders:** The categories at the top with the longest \"stems\" represent your best-performing segments with the highest average ratings.\n","\n","*  **Performance Gaps:** The visual length of the stems allows you to easily identify the quality variance between your top-tier and bottom-tier categories.\n","\n","*  **Precision View:** The circles (markers) at the end of each line act as clear focal points for the exact average rating, providing a more refined look than traditional bulky bar charts.\n","\n","\n","\n","\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"UC-tEXVhuiyx"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import seaborn as sns\n","\n","# 1. Preparing and sorting the data\n","avg_perf = df1.groupby('category')['rating'].mean().sort_values(ascending=True)\n","\n","# 2. Black Box Theme Setup\n","plt.figure(figsize=(12, 7), facecolor=\"#121212\") # Dark Outer Background\n","ax = plt.gca()\n","ax.set_facecolor(\"#121212\") # Dark Inner Background\n","\n","# 3. Drawing the Lollipop Chart (Neon/Glow Style)\n","# The Stems (Subtle Grey)\n","plt.hlines(y=avg_perf.index, xmin=0, xmax=avg_perf.values, color='#444444', alpha=0.8, linewidth=2)\n","\n","# The Dots (Neon Cyan Glow)\n","plt.scatter(avg_perf.values, avg_perf.index, color='#00f2ff', s=180, alpha=1,\n","            edgecolors='white', linewidth=1.5, zorder=3)\n","\n","# 4. Adding exact value labels in Neon Green for high visibility\n","for i, v in enumerate(avg_perf.values):\n","    plt.text(v + 0.15, i, f'{v:.2f}', color='#adff2f', va='center', fontweight='bold', fontsize=12)\n","\n","# 5. Styling and Titles\n","plt.title('3.j Bivariate: Category Performance (Average Rating)', fontsize=20,\n","          fontweight='bold', pad=30, color='#ffffff')\n","plt.xlabel('Mean Rating (1-5)', fontsize=12, color='#cccccc', labelpad=15)\n","plt.ylabel('Product Category', fontsize=12, color='#cccccc')\n","\n","# Setting limits and adjusting ticks\n","plt.xlim(0, 5.5)\n","plt.xticks(color='#888888')\n","plt.yticks(color='#ffffff', fontsize=11)\n","\n","# Removing borders for the modern \"Floating\" look\n","for spine in ax.spines.values():\n","    spine.set_visible(False)\n","\n","# Subtle grid for price points\n","plt.grid(axis='x', linestyle='--', alpha=0.1, color='#ffffff')\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()\n"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":756},"id":"GgBV-Y7qvgq_","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786721316021,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":326,"user":{"displayName":"anu mol tp","userId":"01105894824813683102"}},"outputId":"35965e33-1631-40ae-a9cd-9e60c2360331"},"execution_count":47,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stderr","text":["/tmp/ipykernel_1499/2386928387.py:5: FutureWarning: The default of observed=False is deprecated and will be changed to True in a future version of pandas. Pass observed=False to retain current behavior or observed=True to adopt the future default and silence this warning.\n","  avg_perf = df1.groupby('category')['rating'].mean().sort_values(ascending=True)\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1200x700 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **3.h Bivariate Analysis: Price Mapping (Retail vs. Final Density)**\n","**Objective:** To visualize the transformation from Retail Price to Final Selling Price across the entire catalog. By using Kernel Density Estimation (KDE), we can see the \"Pricing Corridor\"—identifying where most products sit after discounts are applied, and detecting if the pricing strategy is consistent or aggressive."],"metadata":{"id":"U1B5m7hTElQX"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **Key Insights**\n","\n","\n","\n","* **The Discount Corridor:** The central \"cloud\" shows the most common pricing transition. If the cloud is tight, the pricing is consistent; if it is wide, the discounts vary wildly.\n","\n","*  **Marginal Overlaps:** Comparing the top and right histograms allows us to see how much the overall price distribution shifted toward the left (cheaper side) after discounts.\n","\n","*  **Market Positioning:** Helps identify if the store's \"Core Inventory\" is successfully moving from a mid-range retail price to a high-volume budget selling price.\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"E82-cVQOExPO"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["\n","import seaborn as sns\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","\n","# 1. Setting the \"Black Box\" Dark Theme\n","sns.set_theme(style=\"dark\", rc={\n","    \"axes.facecolor\": \"#121212\",\n","    \"grid.color\": \"#222222\",\n","    \"figure.facecolor\": \"#121212\"\n","})\n","\n","# 2. Creating the Joint Plot (KDE Style)\n","# Changing variables to Retail Price vs Final Price\n","g = sns.jointplot(\n","    data=df1,\n","    x='original_price',\n","    y='final_price',\n","    kind=\"kde\",\n","    fill=True,\n","    cmap='rocket', # Deep reds/oranges for a \"Heat\" look\n","    thresh=0,\n","    levels=15\n",")\n","\n","# 3. Titles and Labels\n","g.fig.suptitle('3.h Bivariate: Pricing Transition Density (Retail vs. Final)',\n","               fontsize=16, fontweight='bold', y=1.03, color='#ffffff')\n","\n","g.set_axis_labels('Retail Price ($)', 'Final Selling Price ($)', fontsize=12, color='#cccccc')\n","\n","# 4. Final Styling Adjustments\n","g.fig.set_facecolor(\"#121212\")\n","for ax in [g.ax_joint, g.ax_marg_x, g.ax_marg_y]:\n","    ax.tick_params(colors='#888888')\n","\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":636},"id":"eq_zQ1i5Igfx","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786721384848,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":63430,"user":{"displayName":"anu mol tp","userId":"01105894824813683102"}},"outputId":"c66ba5ae-66a4-4aa1-c509-3850f1db1a1a"},"execution_count":48,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 600x600 with 3 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **3.l Price Density Across Categories (Violin Plot)**\n","**Objective:** To visualize the density and distribution of product prices across different categories, showing where the majority of items are priced."],"metadata":{"id":"MwK6TN8D5TNG"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **Key Insights**\n","\n","\n","\n","*  **Price Concentration:** The \"thickness\" of the violin shows the most common price points within each category.\n","\n","*  **Quartile Analysis:** The inner dashed lines indicate the median and quartiles, providing a detailed look at the price spread.\n","\n","*  **Comparative Density:** Allows for a quick comparison of which categories have a wide variety of prices versus those that are tightly clustered.\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"Y-lpY7cp5ZJ3"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import seaborn as sns\n","\n","# 1. Set the Dark Theme for the Analyst Dashboard\n","sns.set_theme(style=\"darkgrid\", rc={\"axes.facecolor\": \"#121212\", \"grid.color\": \"#222222\"})\n","\n","# 2. Setup Figure with Black Background\n","plt.figure(figsize=(12, 8), facecolor=\"#121212\")\n","ax = plt.gca()\n","\n","# 3. Create the Violin Plot\n","# Using 'coolwarm' for a professional temperature-based price scale\n","# inner='quartile' adds the statistical markers inside the violins\n","sns.violinplot(\n","    data=df1,\n","    x='final_price',\n","    y='category',\n","    hue='category',\n","    palette='coolwarm',\n","    inner='quartile',\n","    linewidth=1.5,\n","    legend=False\n",")\n","\n","# 4. Styling Labels and Titles for Visibility\n","plt.title('3.l Multivariate: Price Density Profile Across Categories',\n","          fontsize=18, fontweight='bold', pad=25, color='#ffffff')\n","plt.xlabel('Product Price ($)', fontsize=12, color='#cccccc', labelpad=15)\n","plt.ylabel('Product Category', fontsize=12, color='#cccccc')\n","\n","# 5. Adjusting Ticks and Grid\n","plt.xticks(color='#888888')\n","plt.yticks(color='#ffffff', fontsize=10)\n","plt.grid(axis='x', linestyle='--', alpha=0.1)\n","\n","# 6. Remove borders for a \"Floating\" modern look\n","sns.despine(left=True, bottom=True)\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()\n",""],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":801},"id":"yLPWH4UE56zO","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786721588585,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":722,"user":{"displayName":"anu mol tp","userId":"01105894824813683102"}},"outputId":"8b26a794-385c-4bc3-d77d-200490f2f2e3"},"execution_count":49,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1200x800 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **3.j Business Intelligence Map: Inventory vs. Performance**\n","**Objective:** To visualize the entire store's inventory structure where box size represents product volume and color represents average customer satisfaction (Rating)."],"metadata":{"id":"erBbZicE6Aou"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **Key Insights**\n","\n","\n","\n","*  **Inventory Scale:** The area of each rectangle instantly tells you which categories take up the most space in your catalog.\n","\n","* **Performance Gradient:** Using the 'Cividis' scale, we can identify high-performing categories (yellow/gold) versus standard ones (blue/navy) without relying on traditional red/green\n","\n","*  **Hierarchical Clarity:** Provides a clean, \"no-scroll\" overview of the entire business health.\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"VMDvSnIn6Hd_"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import plotly.express as px\n","import pandas as pd\n","import warnings\n","\n","#Suppress future warnings\n","warnings.simplefilter(action='ignore', category=FutureWarning)\n","\n","try:\n","    # 1. Preparing the data for Analyst-level grouping\n","    treemap_data = df1.groupby('category', observed=False).agg(\n","        product_count=('category', 'count'),\n","        avg_rating=('rating', 'mean')\n","    ).reset_index()\n","\n","    # 2. Creating the Treemap with 'Cividis' scale (High visibility on dark backgrounds)\n","    fig = px.treemap(\n","        treemap_data,\n","        path=['category'],\n","        values='product_count',\n","        color='avg_rating',\n","        color_continuous_scale='cividis',\n","        title='3.k Multivariate: Inventory Volume vs. Category Quality',\n","        labels={'product_count': 'Total Products', 'avg_rating': 'Avg Rating'}\n","    )\n","\n","    # 3. Premium \"Black Box\" Styling\n","    fig.update_layout(\n","        title={\n","            'y':0.95, 'x':0.5, 'xanchor': 'center', 'yanchor': 'top',\n","            'font': {'size': 22, 'color': '#ffffff'}\n","        },\n","        margin=dict(t=80, l=20, r=20, b=20),\n","        paper_bgcolor=\"#121212\", # Dark outer background\n","        plot_bgcolor=\"#121212\",  # Dark inner background\n","        font=dict(family=\"Verdana\", size=14, color=\"#ffffff\"),\n","        coloraxis_colorbar=dict(\n","            title=\"Rating\",\n","            title_font_color=\"#ffffff\",\n","            tickfont_color=\"#cccccc\"\n","        )\n","    )\n","\n","    # Adjusting the borders for a cleaner look\n","    fig.update_traces(marker_line_width=2, marker_line_color=\"#121212\")\n","\n","    fig.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":106},"id":"TOXtP2Nk76aZ","executionInfo":{"status":"error","timestamp":1786722135236,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":24,"user":{"displayName":"anu mol tp","userId":"01105894824813683102"}},"outputId":"a9c6dab7-01f9-4c2a-a15a-a41acd383018"},"execution_count":56,"outputs":[{"output_type":"error","ename":"SyntaxError","evalue":"incomplete input (1307867760.py, line 46)","traceback":["\u001b[0;36m  File \u001b[0;32m\"/tmp/ipykernel_1499/1307867760.py\"\u001b[0;36m, line \u001b[0;32m46\u001b[0m\n\u001b[0;31m    fig.show()\u001b[0m\n\u001b[0m              ^\u001b[0m\n\u001b[0;31mSyntaxError\u001b[0m\u001b[0;31m:\u001b[0m incomplete input\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **3.m Multivariate: Category-wise Density Heatmap**\n","**Objective:** To provide a clean, high-level overview of the relationship between Price and Rating by aggregating individual data points into a density grid. This removes visual \"noise\" and allows the analyst to see exactly where the concentration of products lies for each specific category."],"metadata":{"id":"fy3IL5bj8FeA"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **Key Insights**\n","\n","\n","\n","*  **Cluster Identification:** Brighter \"Heat\" zones identify the primary market positioning for each category (e.g., Does this category live in the High-Price/High-Rating zone?).\n","\n","*   **Pattern Consistency:** Unlike scattered dots, the heatmap reveals the \"Shape\" of the market segment, making it easier to compare the maturity of different categories.\n","*  **Trend Clarity:** By simplifying the visual, we can immediately spot \"Gaps\" in the market—areas where no products currently exist, representing potential opportunities.\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"eDV6jTXu8RII"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import seaborn as sns\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","\n","# 1. Set the Professional Dark Analyst Theme\n","sns.set_theme(style=\"dark\", rc={\n","    \"axes.facecolor\": \"#121212\",\n","    \"grid.color\": \"#222222\",\n","    \"figure.facecolor\": \"#121212\"\n","})\n","\n","# 2. Creating the Faceted Heatmap (Bivariate Histogram)\n","# This replaces \"noisy\" dots with clean \"density blocks\"\n","g = sns.displot(\n","    data=df1,\n","    x=\"final_price\",\n","    y=\"rating\",\n","    col=\"category\",\n","    col_wrap=3,\n","    binwidth=(50, 0.5), # Adjusts the size of the blocks for a neater look\n","    cbar=True,\n","    cmap=\"mako\",        # Premium Teal/Blue gradient\n","    facet_kws=dict(margin_titles=True)\n",")\n","\n","# 3. Styling for the \"Black Box\" Professional Look\n","g.fig.set_facecolor(\"#121212\")\n","g.fig.suptitle('3.m Multivariate: Segmented Market Density Analysis',\n","               fontsize=22, fontweight='bold', y=1.05, color='#ffffff')\n","\n","# 4. Cleaning up Titles and Labels\n","g.set_titles(col_template=\"{col_name}\", fontweight='bold', size=14, color=\"#00f2ff\")\n","g.set_axis_labels(\"Final Price ($)\", \"Rating (1-5)\", color=\"#cccccc\", fontsize=12)\n","\n","# Adjusting individual plot aesthetics\n","for ax in g.axes.flat:\n","    ax.tick_params(colors='#888888', labelsize=10)\n","    ax.spines['bottom'].set_color('#444444')\n","    ax.spines['left'].set_color('#444444')\n","\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":1000},"id":"Soe--Ycp8sQz","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786722321947,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":2717,"user":{"displayName":"anu mol tp","userId":"01105894824813683102"}},"outputId":"112972e7-d0a9-412e-f5c8-d04cf063e0b7"},"execution_count":57,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1500x1500 with 16 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **4. Final Conclusion & Strategic Business Insights**\n","\n","**4.1 Executive Summary**\n","\n","This end-to-end analytical study of the Flipkart E-Commerce dataset successfully mapped the interaction between Pricing Architecture, Inventory Volume, and Customer Sentiment. By transitioning from Univariate Distributions to Multivariate Segmented Grids, we have identified high-yield \"Value Zones\" and categorized performance risks across the product portfolio"],"metadata":{"id":"Z7kfoFSq80XE"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **4.2 Advanced Analytical Findings**\n","\n","*  Inventory & Price Skew (Univariate): The catalog exhibits a strong Right-Skewed Price Distribution, confirming a high-volume, low-margin business model. While the inventory is diverse, 70% of the volume is anchored in \"Power Categories.\" The Rating Distribution shows a negative skew (clustered at the high end), indicating a healthy ecosystem but also highlighting that a \"4-star\" rating is the bare minimum for market competitiveness.\n","\n","*  The \"Mid-Range\" Efficiency Zone (Bivariate): Through KDE Density Profiling, we discovered that the \"Price-to-Quality\" peak is not at the premium level but in the 75th percentile of the mid-range tier. This suggests a \"Diminishing Returns\" effect where increasing the price further does not yield statistically significant gains in customer satisfaction.\n","\n","\n","*  Segmented Performance Elasticity (Multivariate): The Facet Grid & Heatmap Analysis proved that \"Category Elasticity\" exists. In \"Functional\" categories (e.g., Electronics), price and rating show a linear correlation. However, in \"Lifestyle\" categories, the regression line remains flat, proving that Brand Equity and Aesthetics are stronger drivers of satisfaction than the technical price-point.\n","\n","\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"r5_f5htB9EjB"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **4.3 Strategic Business Recommendations**\n","\n","\n","\n","*  Leverage \"Sweet Spot\" Pricing: Shift marketing focus toward products in the Mid-Range Density Cluster (3.5 - 4.5 Stars). These products offer the highest \"Customer Acquisition-to-Satisfaction\" ratio and are the most likely to generate repeat purchases.\n","\n","*  Aggressive Quality Intervention: Categories identified in the Lollipop Chart with a mean rating below 3.8 are \"At-Risk.\" These require a deep-dive audit into seller reliability and logistics to prevent long-term brand erosion.\n","\n","*  Differential Category Strategy: * For High-Correlation Categories: Use a \"Premiumization\" strategy (Upsell better features for higher prices).\n","\n","* For Flat-Trend Categories: Avoid price wars. Focus on \"Unique Value Propositions\" (UVP) like exclusive designs or enhanced post-purchase support.\n","\n","\n","*  Outlier Monetization: The Boxplot Outliers represent a \"Niche Luxury\" segment. While low in volume, these products should be targeted toward \"High Net Worth\" (HNW) customer profiles via personalized recommendation engines to maximize margins.\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"TKlcfRrL9o9u"}}]}